These three dominoes follow a secret pattern. Look at the relationship between the top numbers and the bottom numbers. What number is missing from the last domino?
$$
\begin{array}{|c|} 
\hline
3 \\
\hline
6 \\
\hline
\end{array}
\hskip{5mm}
\begin{array}{|c|} 
\hline
5 \\
\hline
10 \\
\hline
\end{array}
\hskip{5mm}
\begin{array}{|c|} 
\hline
9 \\
\hline
? \\
\hline
\end{array}
$$

A game piece starts at space A-1. It moves 2 spaces right, but then it hits a magic mirror line on column C that reflects its position perfectly back to column A on the same row. What space does it actually end up on?
$$
\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|}
2 & \text{Room 4} & \text{Room 5} & \text{Room 6} \\
\hline
1 & \text{Start} & \text{Room 2} & \text{Room 3} \\
\hline
 & \text{A} & \text{B} & \text{C}
\end{array}
$$

Look at these three interlocking gears. If Gear 1 spins Clockwise (like the hands of a clock), which way will Gear 3 spin?
$$
\begin{array}{ccccc}
\text{[Gear 1]} & \rightarrow & \text{[Gear 2]} & \rightarrow & \text{[Gear 3]} \\
\text{(Clockwise)} & & & & \mathbf{?}
\end{array}
$$
